   "text": {
    "L1": "Earth has two important movements: rotation and revolution.",
    "L2": "The Sun does not go around Earth each day. Earth rotates, causing day and night.",
    "L3": "Earth spins on its axis from west to east, once in about 24 hours.",
    "L4": "The half facing the Sun has day; the other half has night. As Earth rotates, places move from night into day and back.",
    "L5": "Because Earth rotates west to east, the Sun appears to rise in the east and set in the west.",
    "L6": "Places farther east turn into sunlight first, so sunrise is earlier there.",
    "L7": "Earth also revolves around the Sun. One revolution takes about 365¼ days, which is one year.",
    "L8": "Rotation gives us day and night; revolution gives us the year. The extra quarter day makes a 29 February every fourth year."
   },
